From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crasbe <crasbe@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:30:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] examples/client: include sys/types.h for ssize_t

object_server.c uses the POSIX type ssize_t, but relied on it being
provided transitively by other headers (e.g. <time.h> pulling in
<sys/types.h>). This is not the case for all C libraries, e.g. picolibc
1.8 with -std=c11, so include <sys/types.h> explicitly.
---
 examples/client/object_server.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/examples/client/object_server.c b/examples/client/object_server.c
index a19516d..ff1e142 100644
--- a/examples/client/object_server.c
+++ b/examples/client/object_server.c
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
+#include <sys/types.h>
 
 typedef struct _server_instance_
 {
